claimed: okay-acme -- operator ask 2026-09-07: ACME out of the box. A NEW module okay-acme (JVM, on okayHttp.jvm + okaySecurity.jvm) holding an RFC 8555 client, deliberately narrow: HTTP-01 only, one order over a list of domains, an EC account key kept as PKCS#8 beside the certificate, the directory's staging URL the DEFAULT so a first run cannot burn production rate limits, renewal when the certificate has less than `renewBefore` left. The pieces: the ACME flavour of JWS over Es256 (protected header with nonce/url and jwk-then-kid), the RFC 7638 thumbprint for the key authorization, the state machine (directory, nonce, newAccount, newOrder, authorization, challenge, poll, finalize, download), and the CSR -- openssl, with a NAMED refusal when it is absent, because no exported JDK API builds a PKCS#10. okay-script wires it: OKAY_ACME=<email>, OKAY_ACME_DOMAINS=a,b, OKAY_ACME_PROD=1, the challenge served on the plaintext port BEFORE the https redirect, the issued files picked up by Tls.reloading. Tested against an in-process fake ACME server in the default gate; Pebble interop filed as its own task.
